 "result_text": "`git.refresh()` and `Git.refresh()` now invalidate every `Git` instance's cached `version_info`. I only ran a short check, and it doesn't exercise the stale-cache case, so the fix is untested.\n\nI added a class-level refresh token to `Git` in `git/cmd.py`. `Git.refresh` replaces it on every call. Each instance remembers the token it cached under. When `version_info` is read and the token has changed, the instance drops its cache and re-runs `git version`. The docstring now says the cache is cleared on refresh.\n\nI ran `version_info` on an instance, called `git.refresh()`, and read it again. It returned `(2, 47, 3)` both times. That is the right result when refreshing to the same executable. I did not point it at a different `git` binary, as in the issue's example.\n\nI did not run the test suite.",
